cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "PyIC50: automated, reproducible four-parameter logistic dose-response fitting and IC50 estimation from 96-well plate assays"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "García-Heredia"
    given-names: "José Manuel"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3095-0050"
    affiliation: "Departamento de Bioquímica Vegetal y Biología Molecular, Universidad de Sevilla, Seville 41012, Spain; Instituto de Biomedicina de Sevilla (IBIS)/HUVR/CSIC/Universidad de Sevilla, Hospital Universitario Virgen del Rocío, Ed. IBIS, Avda. Manuel Siurot S/N, Seville 41013, Spain; CIBER de Cáncer (CIBERONC), Instituto de Salud Carlos III, Madrid, Spain"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jmgheredia/PyIC50"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
abstract: "PyIC50 batch-processes folders of raw 96-well plate-reader exports, applies a fixed set of documented quality-control rules and fits a weighted four-parameter logistic (4PL) curve to each drug and cell-line block, producing one consolidated results table, one plot per curve and a note for every block that could not be fitted."
keywords:
  - dose-response
  - IC50
  - four-parameter logistic
  - cell viability
  - pharmacology
  - Python
